    {
      "id": "banner-and-blood",
      "title": "Banner & Blood",
      "playstyle": "Leadership and persistent Named Formations with a Rider mobility branch: maneuvering Grey Riders/Vardai and a concealed Battle Turned East can challenge an opponent's rank commitments.",
      "hypothesis": "Can leadership and Named investments coexist with an actionable Rider flank threat, and does a player choose between a Rider-move Stratagem and a leadership-resolution Stratagem under the one-plan limit?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Late Banner and Banner Singers support Captains/Kings and Named completion; Marched Beneath the Banner Of x3 amplifies a formation containing those classifications. Center Must Hold and Every Banner Turned Toward Them now offer distinct, competing one-Stratagem-per-Battle choices (one copy each).",
        "Followed x3 and The Battle Had Chosen Them x1 reward Named formations. Fifty Men x1, Hundred Shields x2 and First Spear x3 provide physical presence while attachments and Names develop.",
        "Grey Riders x2 can make a basic Rider Attack after their own Maneuver if a legal flanked target exists; Vardai x2 instead spends an ACTION to Move and potentially use its Rider Attack. The Long March x2 waives normal Maneuver Command for Riders, not Actions.",
        "The Battle Turned East x2 can extend a Rider Move (including an Opening Maneuver) once its trigger fires, but competes with the leadership Stratagems for the single hidden plan. Stood Fast With x2 prevents flanking of its Bonded Frontline formation; it does not create a flank or grant an Attack."
      ],
      "combo_packages": [
        {
          "label": "Leadership Strength spike",
          "enablers": [
            "the-late-banner",
            "the-banner-singers",
            "namar",
