    {
      "id": "blood-and-spoils",
      "title": "Blood & Spoils",
      "playstyle": "Shake, Deplete and displace opposing Forces, then exploit weakened defenders with Raider Incursions and attachment disruption while retaining strong Frontline bodies.",
      "hypothesis": "Can repeated Raiders and Shaken/Depleted enablers generate more sustainable Command and effective Strength than direct King/Captain stacking?",
      "combo_notes": [
        "Iron Boars x3 and Red Duelists x3 are alternative Frontline-only ways to Shake an opposing Frontline; they cannot share one Frontline. A prior Shaken marker is not a second bonus for Boars. With a Raider/Skirmisher here, The Trap Closed x2 can now respond to a negative marker from a legal Tactic such as The Line Was Baited, provided the trap was already set.",
        "The Baggage Was Abandoned Exhausts and Shakes a Rear Force; The Crows Came Down can Exhaust an enemy on PLAY and later Shake an Exhausted Force. Salt-Road Reavers convert Shaken to Depleted, while Shared the Spoils With permits movement.",
        "Black Company x2 and River Raiders x2 punish opponent attachment investment. Two Seized the Standard Of Bonds can remove a Bond even without waiting for an enemy condition.",
        "The Line Was Baited gives Depleted only after a legal rearward Move by a Skirmisher-enabled Tactic. If it cannot move the target, neither Depleted nor The Trap Closed triggers. Raider bodies and Rovan provide independent pressure."
      ],
      "combo_packages": [
